[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Slav Defense: Modern Line, 3...dxc4"]
[ECO "D11"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pawn-grab"]
[Themes "regain-the-pawn,passed-pawn"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3...dxc4"]
[Start "slav 3.Nf3"]

3... dxc4 { Takes the pawn and hopes to hold it with ...b5. } 4. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1 so it can take back on c4. } 4... b5 ( 4... Bg4 5. Bxc4 e6 6. O-O ) ( 4... Nf6 5. Bxc4 Bf5 6. Qb3 { The bishop has left c8, so b7 has no guard, and the queen and bishop together also aim at f7. } ) ( 4... Be6 5. Nc3 { Develops and keeps an eye on b5, so Black cannot easily hold the pawn. } ) 5. a4 { Hits the pawn on b5, which holds c4. If it goes, c4 falls too. } 5... e6 ( 5... b4 6. Bxc4 ) 6. axb5 cxb5 7. b3 { Attacks the base of Black's pawns. After bxc4, White has the pawn back and a strong centre. } 7... Bb4+ ( 7... Nf6 8. bxc4 bxc4 9. Bxc4 ) 8. Bd2 Bxd2+ 9. Nbxd2 a5 10. bxc4 b4 11. Bd3 { White's pawns on c4 and d4 control the centre. Plan: castle, then push c5 or e4. Black's passed pawns on a5 and b4 need watching. } *
